## 3. Mechanical pass

    python3 i18n/audits/evidence/es/relay.library/w4a2/checks.py

This script is part of the evidence and reproduces every structural claim below. It writes
nothing and exits non-zero if any check fails.

    exit 1 — RESULT: FAILURES: es plural carries `many` (locale convention 57/58)
    FAIL  es plural carries `many` :: MISSING - exact 10^6 falls back to `other`

That non-zero exit is the finding, not a script error: the script encodes the locale convention,
and this key does not meet it. All other assertions pass (placeholders, categories, parity, hashes).

Supporting census (outside the script):

    all 58 es plural messages -> 57 with {one, many, other}, 1 with {one, other}  <-- this key
    all 105 en plural messages -> {one, other} only


## 4. Semantic pass

Read the English and the Spanish namespace by namespace against the sidecar roles. Judged
accuracy, idiom, register, glossary consistency, placeholder/ICU integrity, plurals, width.
The findings and their reasoning are in `record.json` (structured) and `report.md` (prose).

- The plural is grammatical in both branches and stays lowercase, per the sidecar.
- 'recurso' matches the shipped Library vocabulary (`wire.slash.library.help`: "la Biblioteca global
  de recursos"), so the phone grid and the slash surface name the same thing the same way.
- 'count' is the server's filtered total; the Spanish adds no qualifier that would imply the number
  matches what is painted.
- The one defect is structural: the es `many` branch is absent. Spanish CLDR needs it for exact
  multiples of 10^6, the style guide prescribes it, and 57 of 58 es plural messages have it. At
  exactly 1.000.000 the fallback renders "1.000.000 recursos" instead of "1.000.000 de recursos".

## 5. Judgement

**PASSED** — 1 key read, 1 minor, nothing gating.

Structure and vocabulary are right; the missing es `many` branch is the only defect and it only
manifests at an exact count of one million. Worth fixing in the next pass, not worth blocking the
wave.

